id: flip
name: Flip
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
moveSkill: acrobatics
movePerRank: 2
says: >
  You may move through Squares an Opponent occupies, as long as you do not end your
  movement on an occupied Square. This movement does not provoke the Exploit Maneuver,
  even if you leave the Melee Range of an Opponent.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Tumble clear. Move up to twice your Acrobatics Ranks in Squares, through Opponents if
  you like, and nothing gets a free swing at you for it.
text: >
  Flip Maneuver [1/Round]: Acrobatically maneuver yourself away from your opponent!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Move a number of Squares up to twice your number of Skill Ranks in Acrobatics
  (you may move through Squares occupied by an Opponent, as long as you do not end your
  movement on an occupied Square). This movement does not provoke the Exploit Maneuver,
  even if you leave the Melee Range of an Opponent.

---

# No script. What this Maneuver does is move you, and this system moves nobody - the
# players move the tokens, which is a thing the table settled it would rather keep. So
# what the card can give them is the number and the two sentences that go with it, and
# that is what it gives them.
#
# --- The number -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Twice your number of Skill Ranks in Acrobatics", written as the Skill and the multiplier
# rather than as code: `moveSkill` and `movePerRank`. Read off the character when the
# Maneuver is used, so a Rank gained since the Encounter started counts.
#
# At no Ranks it is nothing, and the card says nothing rather than a zero dressed up as an
# allowance - which is the honest answer: an Acrobatics you never trained buys no Squares.
#
# --- What it does not provoke ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "This movement does not provoke the Exploit Maneuver, even if you leave the Melee Range
# of an Opponent."
#
# Nothing here has to be switched off for that. An Exploit is offered off a card by
# `exploitable`, which is the line the entry prints - and this entry prints "N/A", so there
# is no line and nothing is offered. The Movement Maneuver's line is "If you leave the
# Melee Range of an Opponent", and this is not the Movement Maneuver.
#
# So it is said rather than enforced, and being said is the point: nothing in this system
# watches a token cross a Square, so the only thing that would have provoked an Exploit
# here is somebody at the table remembering that movement usually does. The card tells them
# not to.
#
# --- What is not built --------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Moving through an occupied Square and not stopping on one. Both are about where a token
# is, and nothing here knows or cares - the sentence is carried to the table whole.
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system, which the Arrogant Declaration,
# Analysis, Hype and Brace files all say about their own Minion lines.
#
# --- How it is gained ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Acrobatics, at the 2+ Ranks every Skill grants a Special Maneuver at: "Special Maneuver:
# you gain access to the Flip Maneuver" is in the Skill's own entry.
#
# Which is the same Skill this entry counts for distance - and that is a coincidence of
# this Maneuver rather than a rule. Dirty Trick is a Clash made with Bluff and Bluff opens
# the Feint instead, so the Skill a Maneuver uses and the Skill that hands it over are two
# separate questions with two separate answers. Built from the entry either way, which is
# why the guess being right cost nothing.
